<title>USA: BMW May U.S. car sales rise.</title>
<headline>BMW May U.S. car sales rise.</headline>
<dateline>DETROIT 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bayerische Motoren Werke AG</p>
<p>			May 1-31, 1997     May 1-31, 1996 *Pct Chng</p>
<p> Domestic Car	     1,642	     1,405	    +16.9</p>
<p> Domestic Truck		 0		   0	     N.A.</p>
<p> Import Car		 9,472	     8,053	    +17.6</p>
<p> Import Truck		   0		   0	     N.A.</p>
<p>		  Jan 1-May 31, 1997 Jan 1-May 31, 1996 *Pct Chng</p>
<p> Domestic Car	     9,258	     3,590	   +159.9</p>
<p> Domestic Truck		 0		   0	     N.A.</p>
<p> Import Car		42,108	    35,441	    +19.7</p>
<p> Import Truck		   0		   0	     N.A.</p>
<p>* Pct change based on daily selling rate. Sale days 26 in latest month vs 26, 128 for year to date vs 129 in year ago.</p>
<p>NOTE: Domestic car figures include the Z3 roadster only. Complete sales data not available for U.S.-built 3-Series sedans, which are no longer being produced at BMW's Greer, S.C., assembly plant. The factory now builds Z3 roasters only.</p>
</text>
